  "question": {
    "text": "The largest natural number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> such that <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>n</mi></math> divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>66</mn><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "31",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>We know that,</p><p>Maximum value&nbsp;of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;for&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;where&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi></math>&nbsp;is prime&nbsp;divides the number&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>!</mo></math>&nbsp;is given by,</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><mi>p</mi></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>p</mi><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;is a prime number, so we have</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>66</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>66</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>66</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>3</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>66</mn><msup><mn>3</mn><mn>4</mn></msup></mfrac></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math></p><p>So, maximum value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>31</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
